# ============================================================================
#  spain-dnv-consultant — .gitignore (ALWAYS-ON privacy net)
#
#  This file is the primary, un-bypassable line of defense against committing
#  personal data. Everything you (or a forker) produce while using the engine
#  lives under user/ and is NEVER tracked. Do NOT edit this file to "make git
#  see" your documents — that defeats the whole point. See README "Safety".
# ============================================================================

# ---- user workspace: ALL of it is local; PII never leaves your machine -----
# Ignore everything under user/, but keep the directory itself, its readme,
# and the *.example schema stubs that ship as documentation.
user/**
!user/**/
!user/**/*.example
!user/.gitkeep
!user/README.md
# Documentation-only schema stub that ships next to its *.example (no PII).
# Exact-path exception (not a *.schema.md glob) so a forker's own user/ files
# can never be un-ignored by accident.
!user/pipeline-state.schema.md

# ---- skill output paths (defense-in-depth) ---------------------------------
# Produced by the dnv-* skills. By design they live under user/ (covered
# above). These root-anchored rules also catch a stray write at the repo root
# WITHOUT hiding the synthetic example/ assets that intentionally ship.
/case-profile.json
/pipeline-state.json
/verification_report.md
/spec.md
/claims.json
/drafts/
/slices/

# ---- raw / fresh chat exports (Telegram JSON can be huge and full of PII) ---
*chat*export*.json
*CHAT_ARCHIVE*.json
*CHAT_ACRHIVE*.json
*_chat_texts.json
*_chat_filtered.json

# ---- PII-prone binaries OUTSIDE the shipped surface ------------------------
# The template ships only text. Filled forms, scans, and archives are user
# outputs — never commit them. (The U16 release gate enforces this too.)
*.pdf
*.zip
*.docx
*.doc
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.heic
*.webp

# ---- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ---- engine local config (copied from *.example; may hold case keywords) ----
# config.example.json ships as documentation; the working copy a forker fills
# in (employer/bank keywords, paths) must never be tracked.
config.json
/engine/scripts/config.json

# ---- private maintainer-only PII denylist (input to the release gate) ------
# Compiled list of real values used to verify the build is clean. NEVER ship.
_pii_denylist.txt
_private/

# ---- tooling / OS cruft ----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.claude/worktrees/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
